  "reason": "The best result so far (config_016, acc=0.542) uses multimodal/multiprofile/scgpt/imagenet_vit_l/avgpool/weighted, showing that avgpool+weighted substantially outperforms transformer+concat (0.542 vs 0.507) and transformer+weighted (0.520). The key uncertainty is whether this avgpool+weighted advantage is specific to imagenet_vit_l or generalizes across image encoders. Config_008 is a single-variable change (imagenet_vit_l → resnet50) from the best config, directly testing robustness of the aggregation/fusion finding. If it performs comparably, we confirm avgpool+weighted is the critical design choice and can then pivot to RNA encoder variations; if it degrades, we confirm ViT-L is essential and should focus remaining budget on RNA encoder and profile setting. With 5 experiments left, this clean ablation maximizes information gain per experiment."
}

